& [Objective]
  + promote the smallest effect-free project-assembly nucleus observed in live cantor_scribe into a separately governed reusable Cantor kernel component
  + join explicitly supplied project metadata and source text to the published semantic kernel without granting filesystem or service authority

& [Requirements]
  + [CSPA-001] preserve dictated source and exact selected live-source byte identities before derived formation or Rust implementation
  + [CSPA-002] use published bookend f9dcaebdcd97ece5ada0ba54648fdae7e5a61ea9 as predecessor
  + [CSPA-003] do not modify delete stage normalize copy or otherwise disturb the live C checkout
  + [CSPA-004] implement a separate safe-Rust workspace crate named cantor_sop_project
  + [CSPA-005] accept project package file namespace dependency path and text values only as explicitly supplied in-memory data
  + [CSPA-006] reuse cantor_sop_semantics for source analysis semantic validation manifest construction and deterministic identity
  + [CSPA-007] require portable logical source paths with slash separators no absolute form drive prefix backslash empty dot or parent segments
  + [CSPA-008] enforce 1..256 packages at most2048 files at most2MiB per source at most64MiB aggregate source and at most1000 diagnostics
  + [CSPA-009] refuse duplicate identities semantic set members package/path coordinates and repeated project file coordinates
  + [CSPA-010] refuse unknown supplied machine fields unsupported profiles undeclared file namespaces and malformed identifiers
  + [CSPA-011] preserve partial declarations exact UTF-8 byte spans and attributed source diagnostics while marking incomplete assemblies
  + [CSPA-012] perform whole-snapshot semantic validation only after source parsing is diagnostic-free and convert semantic refusal into an attributed project diagnostic
  + [CSPA-013] produce deterministic domain-separated project input semantic snapshot and result digests
  + [CSPA-014] validate an assembly result by deterministic replay and refuse any tampering
  + [CSPA-015] bind capability kernel.sop.project-assemble through the instance contract while retaining the whole cantor_scribe candidate as held
  + [CSPA-016] statically exclude filesystem path APIs process environment database async transport LSP MCP network provider CLI unsafe and live-effect surfaces
  + [CSPA-017] test constructive multi-package assembly ordering independence partial recovery all bounded refusals strict machine forms and receipt tampering
  + [CSPA-018] independently verify the five selected live-source files still match recorded path byte count and SHA256
  + [CSPA-019] verify focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy format exact workspace cross-host script parsing and recursive evidence gates
  + [CSPA-020] publish only owned source formation implementation tests evidence and intentional transitive manifests
  + [CSPA-021] retain host filesystem loading SQLite query search revision drafts LSP MCP transport provider model execution and live service operation as unresolved separately governed candidates

& [Acceptance]
  + [CSPA-A01] source justification plan solution matrix phase lock and satisfaction signature cross-bind exactly
  + [CSPA-A02] selected-source custody independently replays from the unchanged live checkout
  + [CSPA-A03] focused constructive adversarial static-absence and fresh-process assembly gates pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [CSPA-A04] exact workspace Clippy format dual-host script parse and recursive evidence pass before completion publication
  + [CSPA-A05] integration evidence promotes only the supplied assembly capability while the whole cantor_scribe candidate remains held

& [NonAuthority]
  + supplied logical paths name source documents only and never authorize host path resolution or I/O
  + successful assembly is structural semantic computation and grants no execution installation model provider operator storage transport remote mutation update publication or external-effect authority
